================================================================================
WHY THE TWO NEW MISMATCHES ARE THE EXPECTED FAILURES
================================================================================

=== why the reference's segmentation is the correct one ===

The TinyLlama vocabulary is a SentencePiece *unigram* model: every token has a
log-probability score, and llama.cpp picks the segmentation with the best total
score. The scores below come from the upstream GGUF (gguf-py).

  reference (llama.cpp) '▁d' (-20) + 'on' (-30) + "'" (-180) + 't' (-154) = -384
  repository (greedy)  '▁do' (-141) + 'n' (-157) + "'" (-180) + 't' (-154) = -632

  The reference's segmentation scores -384 against the repository's -632, so
  the reference is right by the model's own scoring and the repository's greedy
  longest match is the defect. This is the 7B/7C work item.

=== the tokenisation of each case, in the vocabulary's own terms ===
  the Greek letter (two byte-fallback tokens) ['<s>', '▁', '<0xCE>', '<0xA9>']
  the emoji (four byte-fallback tokens)      ['<s>', '▁', '<0xF0>', '<0x9F>', '<0x98>', '<0x80>']
  the control token as literal text          ['<s>', '▁', '<', 's', '>']
  the control token parsed by the reference  ['<s>', '<s>']

